on}\" --generation \"{generation}\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --model \"{config.executor.model}\" --reasoning-effort \"{config.executor.reasoningEffort}\" --service-tier \"{config.executor.serviceTier}\" --sandbox-mode \"{config.executor.sandboxMode}\" --timeout-seconds \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"'\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1536:            - \"Fail closed before dispatch unless the rendered containment sections exist, --dir is an isolated linked worktree, the primary worktree is clean, and current-worktree changes are confined to artifact_dir both by name and after every path component is resolved through symlinks; append the recovery-baseline commit to state_log\"\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:1549:            - \"PRE-DISPATCH RULE (read before running the script): when this run is ITSELF a fan-out CLI lineage — config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID / SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK / CODEX_SESSION_ID is present in the environment — the lineage IS the executor. Do NOT run this dispatch script. Perform the iteration in-process instead: read the rendered prompt at {state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md, do the review pass yourself, write the iteration file and the delta, and hand the iteration record to the append gateway (append-mode-event.cjs) exactly as the leaf contract requires, never writing the state log yourself, then continue to post_dispatch_validate.\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:65:  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: \"[optional internal path] - Fan-out lineage artifact override for command-owned single-lineage execution.\"\n.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml:155:  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --