`$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:87:| `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Feed `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:symlink check`, `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` and `command-offer.mjs` | update | T029 to T031 cases, `VO` for `codexHookApproval` |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/spec.md:220:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`, `hook-wiring-check.cjs` and their tests | Modify | Flag value refusal, absent repair line, command-entry marker match |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/spec.md:266:| REQ-020 | `DR5-P2-002`: `hook-wiring-check.cjs` reports `ok` only when a `type: command` entry's `command` runs `node` on the runtime's hook script, and a marker in any other field reads `hook-missing`. |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:74:- **WG9, doctor checks.** `hook-wiring-check.cjs` splits a command into simple commands outside quotes and reads `env`, `bash`, `sh` and `zsh` wrappers. A10 counts only `PASS` copies as expected and names report-only copies apart.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/implementation-summary.md:95:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `agents-md-check.cjs`, `tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | Modified | Quote-aware launch reader, A10 count (WG9) |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:44:- WG9: `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `HWT` is `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `CHK` is `$DS/agents-md-check.cjs` and `CHKT` is `$DS/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:230:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The path, parser and trust fixes carry adversarial cases: a file name with a space, a rename to a name with a space, a checkout with fake code and no marker, a marker inside a quoted `echo` argument and a marker named only in a `description` field. Evidence: `worktree-restore.vitest.ts` and `command-offer.vitest.ts` hold the first three, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `names a runtime whose entry echoes a quoted command` and `names a runtime whose entry only describes the script`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/tasks.md:231:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix rows `plan.md` lists for the no-edit gate and the launch reader each exist in the tests T003 to T005 and T034 add. Evidence: the four wordings run on `attachCommand` and on `isReadOnlyExplainer`, the curly wording runs on `commandMeaningEligible`, and `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` holds `node`, `env`, `/usr/bin/env`, `bash -lc`, `zsh -c`, a flag, a stuck separator and a quoted `echo`. `sh` has no case of its own and shares one list with `bash` and `zsh` at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:241`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/verify-wg5-9.md:19:- T034 PASS (with P2 edges): `hook-wiring-check.cjs:115-268` implements the reader as specified. Single quotes are literal, a backslash escapes inside double quotes and outside quotes, and `&&`, `||`, `;`, `|` and newline separate even when stuck to a word. `env` and `/env` are handled with their `NAME=value` and `-` words, as are leading assignments and `node` flags. `bash`, `sh` and `zsh` with a single-dash `c` flag recurse at most two levels (`:264`). The \"a mention is not a wired hook\" comment is kept (`:103`). The test file only adds cases. The `echo` case would print `ok` under the old reader and each of the seven launches would print `hook-missing`, so all eight are meaningful. Findings 1 and 2 list the edges.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/verify-wg5-9.md:26:1. P2. `hook-wiring-check.cjs:131-178,237-257`: these launches read as wired, but none of them runs the script.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/verify-wg5-9.md:33:2. P2. `hook-wiring-check.cjs:224-243`: these working launches read as `hook-missing`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/verify-wg5-9.md:48:- `node --test` on `doctor-agents-md-contract`, `doctor-setup-contract`, `hook-wiring-check` and `agents-md-check`: 103 pass, 0 fail.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/scratch/verify-wg5-9.md:55:- `hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .`: `ok claude`, `ok codex`, `ok cursor`, `ok devin`, exit 0. I listed every shipped hook command with jq.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/plan.md:60:- **The quote-aware launch reader in `hook-wiring-check.cjs`**: splits a hook command into simple commands outside quotes. Without it, a working wrapper reads as a missing hook.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/plan.md:87:| `runsMarker` in `hook-wiring-check.cjs` | Decides `ok` or `hook-missing` | update: quote-aware reader | `HWT`, `node $DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root .` |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:83:hook-wiring-check pass 8, agents-md-check pass 44, doctor-setup-contract pass 4, doctor-agents-md-contract pass 37, fail 0 in each\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:275:- WG9: `runsMarker` (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:141-146`) splits on spaces and wants the marker right after node at a command start. `rowRuntimeCopies` (`agents-md-check.cjs:651`) subtracts only failed, unmeasured and pointer-missing entries, so report-only INFO entries count as expected.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/017-review-pass-two-remediation/spec.md:314:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `agents-md-check.cjs` and `tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`, `tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` | Modify | Quote-aware launch matcher, A10 count |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:58:`INSTALL-SKILLED.md` now tells a Codex user to approve the project hooks through `/hooks` and lists DSH among seven runtimes. `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` reads the Codex config and prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` or `WARN codex-hooks-unapproved` without printing a hash or writing a file, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` runs it. `hook-wiring-check.cjs` reports `hook-missing <runtime>` for a target repository whose Claude, Codex, Cursor or Devin hook file lacks the prompt entry, and `/doctor:symlink check` runs it. The DSH bundle registers the prompt advisor unless its row flag is `false`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/implementation-summary.md:79:| `DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs`, `DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs` | Created | Read-only prompt-hook wiring check |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:37:- `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `CK` is `$DS/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `CKT` its test `$DS/tests/codex-hook-approval-check.test.cjs`. `HW` is `$DS/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and `HWT` its test `$DS/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:94:- [x] T015 [P] In `SCY`, add `hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"` to `upstream_assets`, add a step after the engine run that runs `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\"`, shows each `hook-missing <runtime>` line and ends with STATUS=WARN on exit 1, naming the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from Skilled's own file for that runtime into the target's file. Append to the invariant that the route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, keeping the words `check subcommand only`. Verify: `rg -c \"hook-wiring-check.cjs\" $SCY` prints at least 2 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/tasks.md:99:- [x] T018 [P] In `$DS/README.markdown`, add `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs` and `hook-wiring-check.cjs` to the tree, the script table and the read-only table, each with its flags and exit codes. Verify: `rg -c \"codex-hook-approval-check.cjs|hook-wiring-check.cjs\" $DS/README.markdown` prints at least 4.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/plan.md:62:- **Hook-wiring check** (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs`): reads the four native hook files of a target repository for the prompt hook entry. `/doctor:symlink check` runs it.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/010-reachability-and-attribution/spec.md:181:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs` and its