{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761284704,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01bda88001jivzAAWb6nAiYZ","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e01bbed4001QxSJ9JSqTTNzIA","type":"tool","id":"call_9c7853c602e24facab10350e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":120,"offset":40,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 40-159\n40: 6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n41: 7. **Emit.** Native adapters emit a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON envelope. OpenCode appends to `output.system` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`. Pi sends a model-visible message.\n42: \n43: The injected brief begins with `Advisor:` and names the routed skill or, when the recommendation resolves to a command, the skill that owns it and the runnable command. A doctor command appears as its runnable `/doctor:` string on the top line or under a skill as an `Also:` second line. The line under a skill reads `Also: <command> (<policy>)`, and it is left out when the head or its partner already names that command. The handler returns `{}` when the hook is disabled, input cannot be parsed or an unhandled exception occurs. A shim also returns `{}` when it cannot resolve or relay valid child output, including on timeout. When the handler has no brief, it emits the directives fallback.\n44: \n45: ### Brief head form\n46: \n47: A recommendation that resolves to a command renders one label, shared by the `use` and `ambiguous` heads:\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: <ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The recommendation's own `ownerSkillId`, `command` and `policy` are authoritative, and the generated command row fills only what they omit. The policy parenthesis is dropped when no policy is known. A recommendation with no command row keeps its skill label rather than a command label.\n54: \n55: The `use` head reads `Advisor: <freshness>; use <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` For example:\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: A hub whose compiled route defers or asks to clarify, and whose modes have commands, renders as `<hub> (needs a mode)` with no command, for example:\n64: \n65: ```text\n66: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.82/0.20 pass.\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The recommendation carries `needsMode: true`. A command on the same recommendation wins and the label is dropped.\n70: \n71: ### Degraded contract\n72: \n73: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n74: \n75: - A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n76: - Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n77: \n78: Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n83: \n84: Every native runtime, Pi and DSH run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n85: \n86: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n87: |---|---|---|---|---|\n88: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n89: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n90: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n91: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n92: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n93: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n94: | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` (real file, reached through the `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` symlink) | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n95: | **Vibe** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`, called by `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs` | `pre_agent` in `.vibe/hooks.toml` (`turn-start`, match `main`), rendered into a dispatch's `VIBE_HOME` | Proxies the operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `vibe`. A child dispatch and a subagent turn get no brief | `hook_specific_output.additional_context`; the routing head and directives repeat only when they change, because Vibe keeps added context in the conversation. A head that names a command gains one line naming each command's document under `.skilled/commands/`, because Vibe has no command loader and its prompt stubs name the dash form |\n96: \n97: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n98: \n99: ### Starting a surfaced command\n100: \n101: The document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n102: \n103: | Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n104: |---|---|---|\n105: | Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists | The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name |\n106: | Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n107: | Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n108: | Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n109: | Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n110: | OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\n111: | DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n119: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n120: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n121: +-- claude/\n122: |   +-- README.md\n123: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n124: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n125: +-- dsh/\n126: |   +-- README.md\n127: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n128: +-- pi/\n129: |   +-- README.md\n130: |   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n131: +-- vibe/\n132: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real Vibe part (the turn-start composer calls it)\n133: `-- lib/\n134:     +-- README.md\n135:     +-- directive-lifecycle.ts, directive-lifecycle-contract.ts, directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts\n136:     +-- directive-lifecycle-store.py, directive-lifecycle-vectors.json\n137:     `-- skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts\n138: \n139: system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.{ts,js}  # thin shims (claude/codex/cursor/devin)\n140: system-skill-advisor/runtime/\n141: +-- dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js   # compiled advisor the shims spawn\n142: +-- lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts, render.ts, metrics.ts, subprocess.ts\n143: `-- scripts/skill_advisor.py                      # standalone Python advisor CLI\n144: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js         # OpenCode plugin\n145: ```\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 5. KEY FILES\n150: \n151: | File | Responsibility |\n152: |---|---|\n153: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n154: | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Thin process-boundary shims. Resolve the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor, spawn the compiled advisor with bounded stdin/stdio/timeout, and relay its stdout (or `{}` on any failure). |\n155: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n156: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n157: | `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` | The CLI front door the OpenCode plugin spawns. Receives the `advisor_recommend` command line, returns the JSON payload on stdout. |\n158: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts` | The brief builder: scoring, freshness, status, confidence/uncertainty. |\n159: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | `renderAdvisorBrief` / `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`, produces the model-visible text. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 160]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 40-159\n40: 6. **Directive-lifecycle dedup.** `decideDirectiveLifecycleDelivery` suppresses a re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence, so a repeated prompt does not re-inject an identical brief. A repeat in a known session keeps the first line, a route or a fallback status, and drops the directives block.\n41: 7. **Emit.** Native adapters emit a `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON envelope. OpenCode appends to `output.system` via `experimental.chat.system.transform`. Pi sends a model-visible message.\n42: \n43: The injected brief begins with `Advisor:` and names the routed skill or, when the recommendation resolves to a command, the skill that owns it and the runnable command. A doctor command appears as its runnable `/doctor:` string on the top line or under a skill as an `Also:` second line. The line under a skill reads `Also: <command> (<policy>)`, and it is left out when the head or its partner already names that command. The handler returns `{}` when the hook is disabled, input cannot be parsed or an unhandled exception occurs. A shim also returns `{}` when it cannot resolve or relay valid child output, including on timeout. When the handler has no brief, it emits the directives fallback.\n44: \n45: ### Brief head form\n46: \n47: A recommendation that resolves to a command renders one label, shared by the `use` and `ambiguous` heads:\n48: \n49: ```text\n50: <ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)\n51: ```\n52: \n53: The recommendation's own `ownerSkillId`, `command` and `policy` are authoritative, and the generated command row fills only what they omit. The policy parenthesis is dropped when no policy is known. A recommendation with no command row keeps its skill label rather than a command label.\n54: \n55: The `use` head reads `Advisor: <freshness>; use <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` For example:\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: Advisor: live; use system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start) 0.89/0.12 pass.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: The ambiguous head applies the same label to both sides: `Advisor: <freshness>; ambiguous: <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> vs <label> <confidence>/<uncertainty> pass.` Each label part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`, so a control character, a line break or an instruction-shaped label renders nothing rather than reaching the model. The `Also:` line still names a doctor command by its runnable string.\n62: \n63: A hub whose compiled route defers or asks to clarify, and whose modes have commands, renders as `<hub> (needs a mode)` with no command, for example:\n64: \n65: ```text\n66: Advisor: live; use system-deep-loop (needs a mode) 0.82/0.20 pass.\n67: ```\n68: \n69: The recommendation carries `needsMode: true`. A command on the same recommendation wins and the label is dropped.\n70: \n71: ### Degraded contract\n72: \n73: When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI runs the local Python scorer and returns `status: ok` with `degraded: true` and `source: local-scorer`. The local scorer returns command row ids, which a reader cannot type, so the CLI rewrites each row before the brief renders:\n74: \n75: - A row whose bare slash command appears in the prompt (the row's `command` text before the first space) keeps its command fields: `skillId` is the row id, `kind` is `command`, `command` is the runnable string, `policy` is present when the row has one and `ownerSkillId` names the owning skill. A typed `/speckit:save this session` renders `system-spec-kit → /speckit:save (start)`.\n76: - Every other row collapses to its owner skill: `skillId` is `ownerSkillId` and `kind` is `skill`. It is dropped when that skill is already offered, so the degraded brief never repeats a skill.\n77: \n78: Rows below the threshold are discarded before either rule applies. The degraded brief therefore keeps the same head form and names a skill that exists rather than a raw row id.\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 3. PER-RUNTIME DELIVERY\n83: \n84: Every native runtime, Pi and DSH run the same hook handler, which gates the prompt, calls the advisor CLI and renders with `renderAdvisorBrief`. The OpenCode plugin calls the CLI itself. The native adapters differ in prompt event, transport and delivery channel.\n85: \n86: | Runtime | Adapter | Event / wiring | Payload difference it handles | Delivery |\n87: |---|---|---|---|---|\n88: | **Claude** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `system-skill-advisor/.../dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.claude/settings.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 3s | Shim resolves the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor (install-anchored, not CWD-relative). Bounded stdin (1 MiB), bounded child stdio, 2.5s child timeout, `SIGKILL` on timeout | `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` JSON on stdout. `{}` on any failure |\n89: | **Codex** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.codex/hooks.json`, timeout 3s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope on resolution failure | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n90: | **Cursor** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/cursor/user-prompt-submit.js` | `beforeSubmitPrompt` in `.cursor/hooks.json`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n91: | **Devin** | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.ts` (shim) → `.../dist/hooks/devin/user-prompt-submit.js` | `UserPromptSubmit` in `.devin/hooks.v1.json`, matcher `\"\"`, timeout 10s | Same shim dispatch. `cd \"${DEVIN_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\"`. Fallback `printf` envelope | Same `additionalContext` JSON |\n92: | **Pi** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` (real file, re-exported by its one-line `.pi/extensions/` entry) | `user_input` / prompt event via `.pi/extensions/` | Imports the advisor module **in-process** (not a subprocess). Pi awaits input handlers before agent processing, so the old blocking-spawn bridge stalled every send. In-process calls remove the stall and let the module-level prompt cache work. Captures raw user text (bounded 32 KiB, 64-session LRU). The in-process call passes `runtime: 'pi'` and races a timer of the advisor budget plus 300 ms, delivering the fallback directives if the call hangs | Model-visible message. Delivery-state machine suppresses same-session re-delivery |\n93: | **OpenCode** | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | Plugin, loaded by OpenCode's flat glob over `.opencode/plugins/`. `experimental.chat.system.transform` per prompt, `event` for session lifecycle, `tool` for status | Shells out to the advisor CLI (bounded timeout, stdout cap 256 KiB, grace termination), TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup, transform-dedup integration | Brief appended to `output.system`. `spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` tool returns a key=value report (no raw path leakage) |\n94: | **DSH** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` (real file, reached through the `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/prompt-advisor.mjs` symlink) | `agent/pre-step` through the `repo-guards` plugin, on unless the `promptAdvisor` row flag is `false` | Proxies the latest operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `dsh`. A fan-out leaf, marked by the lineage patch, gets no brief | Brief added to the step |\n95: | **Vibe** | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs`, called by `.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs` | `pre_agent` in `.vibe/hooks.toml` (`turn-start`, match `main`), rendered into a dispatch's `VIBE_HOME` | Proxies the operator prompt through the compiled Claude advisor chain under the runtime label `vibe`. A child dispatch and a subagent turn get no brief | `hook_specific_output.additional_context`; the routing head and directives repeat only when they change, because Vibe keeps added context in the conversation. A head that names a command gains one line naming each command's document under `.skilled/commands/`, because Vibe has no command loader and its prompt stubs name the dash form |\n96: \n97: OpenCode has no source-hook adapter in `system-spec-kit`. Its prompt-time integration is the committed plugin, which shells out to the advisor CLI and inherits the shared render contract. The hooks-tree index at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/` mirrors the per-runtime shims and the OpenCode plugin via relative symlinks. This README is the symlink target.\n98: \n99: ### Starting a surfaced command\n100: \n101: The document behind a surfaced command is `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md`. The model reads that document in full and follows it, on every runtime. It never tells the user to type a slash command, and it asks the user to type one only when it cannot read the file.\n102: \n103: | Runtime | Model can start a command itself | Basis |\n104: |---|---|---|\n105: | Claude Code | Yes, through the Skill tool, as a shortcut for the names it lists | The Skill tool lists names, not files. A command file named `skill.md` in any capitalisation makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill, an open upstream bug, so no command file carries that name |\n106: | Codex | No | The mirror is a pointer stub that tells the model to read the command file. There is no `.codex/skills` |\n107: | Cursor | No model path found, and the brief is dormant | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Cursor docs were not fetched |\n108: | Devin | No command surface at all | Skills are exposed, commands are not |\n109: | Pi | No model path found | The mirror is a pointer stub. Public Pi docs were not fetched, so this is unverified beyond the repository |\n110: | OpenCode | No documented model path. A parent process can start one with `opencode run --command` | Commands are user-triggered templates, while skills are loaded by the model through a skill tool |\n111: | DSH | No | dsh has no agent-file loader and no command loader |\n112: \n113: ---\n114: \n115: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: system-skill-advisor/hooks/\n119: +-- skill-advisor-hook.md            # this reference (symlinked from .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/README.md)\n120: +-- skill-advisor-hook-validation.md # validation/audit detail\n121: +-- claude/\n122: |   +-- README.md\n123: |   +-- directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts\n124: |   `-- user-prompt-submit.ts         # real advisor handler (Claude shape)\n125: +-- dsh/\n126: |   +-- README.md\n127: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real DSH adapter (.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/ imports it)\n128: +-- pi/\n129: |   +-- README.md\n130: |   `-- prompt-advisor.ts             # real Pi extension (.pi/extensions/ re-exports it)\n131: +-- vibe/\n132: |   `-- prompt-advisor.mjs            # real Vibe part (the turn-start composer calls it)\n133: `-- lib/\n134:     +-- README.md\n135:     +-- directive-lifecycle.ts, directive-lifecycle-contract.ts, directive-lifecycle-file-store.ts\n136:     +-- directive-lifecycle-store.py, directive-lifecycle-vectors.json\n137:     `-- skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts\n138: \n139: system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.{ts,js}  # thin shims (claude/codex/cursor/devin)\n140: system-skill-advisor/runtime/\n141: +-- dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js   # compiled advisor the shims spawn\n142: +-- lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts, render.ts, metrics.ts, subprocess.ts\n143: `-- scripts/skill_advisor.py                      # standalone Python advisor CLI\n144: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js         # OpenCode plugin\n145: ```\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 5. KEY FILES\n150: \n151: | File | Responsibility |\n152: |---|---|\n153: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts` | The real advisor handler (Claude shape). Builds the brief, runs the CLI fallback, renders, applies directive-lifecycle dedup, emits the `additionalContext` envelope, persists a diagnostic record. The codex/cursor/devin siblings share the same advisor core over their runtime's payload shape. |\n154: | `system-spec-kit/.../hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.ts` | Thin process-boundary shims. Resolve the advisor target by walking up to the `.opencode` ancestor, spawn the compiled advisor with bounded stdin/stdio/timeout, and relay its stdout (or `{}` on any failure). |\n155: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts` | Native Pi extension. Imports the advisor module in-process, captures raw user text (bounded LRU), runs a delivery-state machine that suppresses same-session re-delivery, and sends the brief as a model-visible message. Races the advisor call against a deadline of the advisor budget plus 300 ms and delivers the fallback directives if it hangs. |\n156: | `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` | OpenCode plugin. `experimental.chat.system.transform` spawns the bridge and appends the brief to `output.system`. `event` manages session lifecycle and cache invalidation. `tool: spec_kit_skill_advisor_status` returns a sanitized status report. TTL+LRU prompt cache with in-flight dedup and transform-dedup integration. |\n157: | `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs` | The CLI front door the OpenCode plugin spawns. Receives the `advisor_recommend` command line, returns the JSON payload on stdout. |\n158: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts` | The brief builder: scoring, freshness, status, confidence/uncertainty. |\n159: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts` | `renderAdvisorBrief` / `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`, produces the model-visible text. |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 160]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":120,\"offset\":40,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761284232,"end":1794761284704}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794761285732,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"id":"prt_1e01be064001B7ElT5QzVWRnem","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e01bbed4001QxSJ9JSqTTNzIA","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"8ee72b1c7ef827f8972a46704055fb057cc13fb2","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":664,"output":89,"reasoning":288,"cache":{"read":202752,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761290552,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"id":"prt_1e01bf338001U6uUZNXprfS7SA","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e01be06a001fuW2ECBDs11pGM","type":"step-start","snapshot":"015c978adf1efe1bab9cd678f525168a56229149"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761293756,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01bfdf1001sa7oVDHXtOcWX2","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e01be06a001fuW2ECBDs11pGM","type":"tool","id":"call_df499825e39341438ae7d018","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":110,"offset":160,"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 160-263\n160: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n161: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n162: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Standalone Python advisor CLI. The advisor CLI runs it as the local scorer when the daemon is unreachable. The hook never calls it directly. |\n163: \n164: ---\n165: \n166: ## 6. CONFIGURATION\n167: \n168: The advisor is enabled by default. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive) for the shared resolver.\n169: \n170: | Variable | Effect |\n171: |---|---|\n172: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Canonical kill-switch. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output, and the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstains. |\n173: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n174: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n175: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters and the `advisor_recommend` direct call. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n176: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n177: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n178: \n179: The direct call decides in the caller's own process, by the same resolution the adapters use. `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` asks `hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor')` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`, with the caller's environment over `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, before it connects to a daemon or runs the local scorer. Whenever the adapters are off, under any name in this table or its older `MK_` form, any truthy value or a line in the flags file, it prints the empty envelope with `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and names the switch that decided. A daemon reads the same names from its own environment and never reads the flags file, and the launcher passes no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` to a daemon it starts, so a flagged command that happens to start the daemon does not leave it abstaining for every later caller. The standalone Python CLI keeps its own rule: only `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, set to exactly `1`.\n180: \n181: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (kept for existing configs: the transform adds no compiled-route line, so it changes only the `bounded_compiled_route_summary` status field).\n182: \n183: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n184: \n185: ---\n186: \n187: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n188: \n189: | Boundary | Rule |\n190: |---|---|\n191: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n192: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n193: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n194: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n195: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n196: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n197: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n198: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n199: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n200: \n201: ### Operator freshness states\n202: \n203: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n204: | --- | --- | --- |\n205: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n206: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n207: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n208: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: ## 8. VALIDATION\n213: \n214: Build both maintained packages:\n215: \n216: ```bash\n217: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build\n218: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n219: ```\n220: \n221: Expected result: both builds succeed and `dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js` are produced.\n222: \n223: ```bash\n224: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck\n225: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n226: node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\n227: ```\n228: \n229: Expected result: no type errors. All advisor package tests pass. The OpenCode plugin test passes.\n230: \n231: Native smoke tests (each targets an existing compiled file):\n232: \n233: ```bash\n234: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"update documentation with DQI checks\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\"}' | \\\n235:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n236: ```\n237: \n238: Expected: `{}` or `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` beginning with `Advisor:`. Repeat for the `codex`, `cursor`, and `devin` siblings.\n239: \n240: OpenCode plugin CLI smoke test:\n241: \n242: ```bash\n243: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"save this conversation context to memory\",\"options\":{\"topK\":3,\"includeAttribution\":false,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true,\"confidenceThreshold\":0.8,\"uncertaintyThreshold\":0.35}}' \\\n244:   | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json\n245: ```\n246: \n247: Installation drift check (from a linked worktree with the required worktree flag):\n248: \n249: ```bash\n250: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree\n251: ```\n252: \n253: This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n254: \n255: ---\n256: \n257: ## 9. RELATED\n258: \n259: - [`skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`](skill-advisor-hook-validation.md): validation and audit detail for this concern.\n260: - [`claude/README.md`](claude/README.md), [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md), [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md): per-surface detail.\n261: - [`../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md`](../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md): the owning skill's hook contract (where the shims live).\n262: - [`../../../hooks/README.md`](../../../hooks/README.md): the unified hooks tree with the kill-switch index and coverage matrix.\n263: - [`../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md`](../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md): the OpenCode plugins folder that loads `system-skill-advisor.js`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md, lines 160-263\n160: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle.ts` | Directive-lifecycle dedup: decides whether a directive should be re-delivered to a session within its cadence. |\n161: | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli` is the hook's CLI caller. It runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` with the hook timeout and sends the request on stdin. The CLI owns daemon startup and local-scorer fallback. The function resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root. It searches `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second. |\n162: | `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Standalone Python advisor CLI. The advisor CLI runs it as the local scorer when the daemon is unreachable. The hook never calls it directly. |\n163: \n164: ---\n165: \n166: ## 6. CONFIGURATION\n167: \n168: The advisor is enabled by default. Truthy disable values are `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` (case-insensitive) for the shared resolver.\n169: \n170: | Variable | Effect |\n171: |---|---|\n172: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` | Canonical kill-switch. Every adapter checks `isHookEnabled('skill-advisor')` and returns empty/skipped prompt-safe output, and the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstains. |\n173: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables the native adapters and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n174: | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Alias. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n175: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias for the native adapters and the `advisor_recommend` direct call. The standalone Python CLI (`skill_advisor.py`) reads only this name, set to exactly `1`, from `runtime/schemas/compat-contract.json`. |\n176: | `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` | Legacy alias. Disables every adapter and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. |\n177: | `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` | Master switch that disables this concern along with every other repo hook. |\n178: \n179: The direct call decides in the caller's own process, by the same resolution the adapters use. `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` asks `hookFlagDecision('skill-advisor')` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`, with the caller's environment over `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env`, before it connects to a daemon or runs the local scorer. Whenever the adapters are off, under any name in this table or its older `MK_` form, any truthy value or a line in the flags file, it prints the empty envelope with `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and names the switch that decided. A daemon reads the same names from its own environment and never reads the flags file, and the launcher passes no switch name and no `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` to a daemon it starts, so a flagged command that happens to start the daemon does not leave it abstaining for every later caller. The standalone Python CLI keeps its own rule: only `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, set to exactly `1`.\n180: \n181: Additional controls: `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_FORCE_LOCAL=1` (force local Python fallback where supported) and `--force-native` / `--force-local` / `--threshold` / `--stdin` (Python shim flags, default threshold `0.8`). `SPECKIT_OPENCODE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` (default 3000) is owned by the `system-skill-advisor` hub: its live consumers are `runtime/lib/subprocess.ts`, `skill-advisor-brief.ts`, the OpenCode bridge and `skill_advisor.py`. On timeout the OpenCode bridge serves prompt-safe stale context with a timeout marker. OpenCode tuning: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_CACHE_TTL_MS` (default 5 min), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_TOKENS` (default 80), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_BRIEF_CHARS` (default 2 KiB), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_MAX_PROMPT_BYTES` (default 64 KiB, measured on the whole stdin request after JSON escaping), `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` (kept for existing configs: the transform adds no compiled-route line, so it changes only the `bounded_compiled_route_summary` status field).\n182: \n183: Set a flag inline for one command, export it for a session, or persist it in `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (copied from `hook-flags.env.example`, gitignored). The environment always wins over the file, so a persisted default can be overridden for a single session.\n184: \n185: ---\n186: \n187: ## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n188: \n189: | Boundary | Rule |\n190: |---|---|\n191: | Advisory only | Hooks surface prompt-safe routing context. They do not replace explicit skill loading, persist raw prompt text, or block the user prompt on advisor failures. |\n192: | Fail-open | All adapters let the prompt proceed. A failed or empty advisor call yields the directives fallback. A parsing failure or unhandled error yields `{}`. The shims return `{}` on `TARGET_UNRESOLVED`, `CHILD_TIMEOUT`, `NONZERO_EXIT`, `EMPTY_OUTPUT`, `INVALID_JSON`, `INPUT_OVERFLOW`, and `SPAWN_ERROR`. |\n193: | Freshness | Freshness states `live`, `stale`, `absent`, `unavailable`. Status values `ok`, `skipped`, `degraded`, `fail_open`. Default confidence/uncertainty `0.8 / 0.35` unless overridden. |\n194: | Privacy | Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution. The OpenCode status tool sanitizes paths (`[configured-node]`, `[skill-advisor-bridge]`). |\n195: | Dedup | Directive-lifecycle dedup suppresses re-delivery of the same directive to the same session within its cadence. OpenCode adds transform-dedup across co-resident transforms. The plugin decides same-message transform dedup on the full advisor block before lifecycle reduction, so a repeated transform for the same message is suppressed. |\n196: | Diagnostics | Each hook record carries `runtime` (the Codex, Cursor and Devin adapters set `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` and Pi passes `pi`) plus `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. Every prompt writes a health record to the diagnostics sink with no prompt, skill label or error text, and an answer from the CLI's local scorer carries `degraded: true`. `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The subprocess hook waits up to 100 ms for pending writes before exit. |\n197: | Bounded | Shims bound stdin (1 MiB), child stdio (1 MiB), child timeout (2.5s), and `SIGKILL` on timeout. OpenCode bounds bridge stdout (256 KiB) and uses grace termination. Pi bounds captured user text (32 KiB, 64-session LRU). |\n198: | Output | Native adapters emit one `additionalContext` JSON on stdout. OpenCode appends to `output.system`. Pi sends a model-visible message. No adapter writes to the TUI prompt line. |\n199: | Imports | Shims import Node builtins only and spawn the advisor by absolute path. The advisor core imports its `runtime/lib/*` siblings and the shared `hook-flags` resolver. Nothing outside the repo. |\n200: \n201: ### Operator freshness states\n202: \n203: | State | Meaning | Operator Action |\n204: | --- | --- | --- |\n205: | `live` | Current graph generation is trusted. | No action. |\n206: | `stale` | Sources are newer than graph state. | Use scored recommendations with a caveat, then rebuild. |\n207: | `absent` | Required graph state is missing. | Rebuild. Empty recommendations are expected until repaired. |\n208: | `unavailable` | Status cannot be read. | Inspect daemon logs and use a supported fallback. |\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: ## 8. VALIDATION\n213: \n214: Build both maintained packages:\n215: \n216: ```bash\n217: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build\n218: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n219: ```\n220: \n221: Expected result: both builds succeed and `dist/hooks/<runtime>/user-prompt-submit.js` are produced.\n222: \n223: ```bash\n224: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run typecheck\n225: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime test -- --reporter=default\n226: node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\n227: ```\n228: \n229: Expected result: no type errors. All advisor package tests pass. The OpenCode plugin test passes.\n230: \n231: Native smoke tests (each targets an existing compiled file):\n232: \n233: ```bash\n234: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"update documentation with DQI checks\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\"}' | \\\n235:   node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js\n236: ```\n237: \n238: Expected: `{}` or `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` beginning with `Advisor:`. Repeat for the `codex`, `cursor`, and `devin` siblings.\n239: \n240: OpenCode plugin CLI smoke test:\n241: \n242: ```bash\n243: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"save this conversation context to memory\",\"options\":{\"topK\":3,\"includeAttribution\":false,\"includeAbstainReasons\":true,\"confidenceThreshold\":0.8,\"uncertaintyThreshold\":0.35}}' \\\n244:   | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json\n245: ```\n246: \n247: Installation drift check (from a linked worktree with the required worktree flag):\n248: \n249: ```bash\n250: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs --check --allow-worktree\n251: ```\n252: \n253: This compares the repository's maintained Codex registration and adapter paths. A report about the user-global installation is workstation state, not a repository defect.\n254: \n255: ---\n256: \n257: ## 9. RELATED\n258: \n259: - [`skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`](skill-advisor-hook-validation.md): validation and audit detail for this concern.\n260: - [`claude/README.md`](claude/README.md), [`pi/README.md`](pi/README.md), [`lib/README.md`](lib/README.md): per-surface detail.\n261: - [`../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md`](../../system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/README.md): the owning skill's hook contract (where the shims live).\n262: - [`../../../hooks/README.md`](../../../hooks/README.md): the unified hooks tree with the kill-switch index and coverage matrix.\n263: - [`../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md`](../../../../.opencode/plugins/README.md): the OpenCode plugins folder that loads `system-skill-advisor.js`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":110,\"offset\":160,\"path\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761293297,"end":1794761293756}}}}
