{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761557908,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02005cb001v7fFXK3owy9dYH","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e01ff3f70011hWmZvMhWUJmUE","type":"tool","id":"call_c79edb88b91c42e5a17a1fa8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":80,"offset":55,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md, lines 55-134\n55: \n56: ## 3. Verifier verdicts and outcome per finding\n57: \n58: Round one, from `review/verify-4/report.md`. The task column names the phase 027 task that fixed the finding, and the decision column names the row in `decision-record.md` for a finding that was not built.\n59: \n60: | Finding | Severity raised | Verifier verdict | Outcome | Task or decision |\n61: |---------|-----------------|------------------|---------|------------------|\n62: | SA4-P1-002 | P1 | Confirmed P1: a refusal over `A or B` keeps the second command | Fixed. The three or-list refusals now carry no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:2-4`) | T004 |\n63: | SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n64: | SA4-P1-003 | P1 | Confirmed, deliberate tradeoff, P2: broad creation words in a correction | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n65: | SA4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` keeps the command | Fixed. The question now carries no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:7`) | T005 |\n66: | SA4-P2-002 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `advisor-recommend.md:39` and the lead row's command | Fixed in the feature catalog page | T014 |\n67: | SA4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the meaning anchor test has 28 cases, not 17 | Fixed | T015 |\n68: | SA4-P2-004 | P2 | Confirmed P2: phase 020 says the weak-cue bar is 10, the code uses 9 | Closed by a superseding note in the phase 027 spec, phase 020 not edited | P048 |\n69: | SA4-P2-005 | P2 | Confirmed P2: no test row for the residual behaviours | Fixed by the rows T004 and T005 added | T004, T005 |\n70: | R4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the Codex reader opens the caller's path after containment resolved another | Fixed, the reader opens the resolved path (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:43`) | T010 |\n71: | R4-P2-002 | P2 | Rejected: the first returned row always leads | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n72: | R4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the advisor README should name `parent-named only` | Fixed | T016 |\n73: | iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | P1 | Confirmed P1: both run-log writers drop `offeredAs` | Fixed in both writers (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:39`) | T006, T007 |\n74: | iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated | P1 | Rejected: a move from 8 to 9 already fails the suite | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n75: | iter1-P2-heredoc-delimiter | P2 | Confirmed P2: an end word with `-` or `.` is read as a command | Fixed, every heredoc line reads `improvised` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:27-32`) | T008 |\n76: | iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start | P2 | Confirmed, raised to P1: a shell `cat` of a command document is not a start | Fixed, and every stored arm rescored (`scratch/rescore-delta.txt`) | T009, T021 |\n77: | iter2-P2-live-holdout-guard-baseline-only | P2 | Confirmed P2: the guard reads the committed baseline only | Fixed, the guard reads the live capture too | T011 |\n78: | iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned | P2 | Rejected: the slice test compares the whole block | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n79: | iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows | P2 | Confirmed P2: the paired block needs a shared owned row | Deferred to phase 026 task T030 | P046 |\n80: | iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision | P2 | Confirmed P2, hand-written logs only: reserve `paired` | Deferred to phase 026 task T053 | P046 |\n81: | iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field | P2 | Confirmed P2: delete the field | Deferred to phase 026 task T052 | P046 |\n82: | DR4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the A11 row should name the by-hand fix for a malformed row | Fixed | T017 |\n83: | The README statement, ungraded | not raised | Seen outside the 21, not graded: `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` heads `/create:readme (start)` | Recorded as a route vocabulary gap at P2, not fixed (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:8`) | P047 |\n84: \n85: Rounds 4b and 4c, adjudicated by the coordinator in `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`:\n86: \n87: | Finding | Round | Severity | Adjudication | Outcome | Task or reason |\n88: |---------|-------|----------|--------------|---------|----------------|\n89: | SAC4B-P1-001 | 4b | P1 | Reproduced: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `868b185e76`, the line now prints no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:9`) | T028 |\n90: | SAC4B-P2-001 | 4b | P2 | Reproduced: a question over an or-list printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `868b185e76` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:12-13`) | T029 |\n91: | SAC4B-P2-002 | 4b | P2 | Retracted by its own lineage: the evidence was an `rg -r` artifact | Resolved in the lineage, no task | Retracted |\n92: | AR4B-P2-001 | 4b | P2 | Confirmed by reading: the README said the backfill adds three fields | Fixed in `868b185e76` | T030 |\n93: | AR4B-P2-002 | 4b | P2 | Confirmed by reading: a head-moved run line carries none of the four fields | Fixed in `868b185e76` | T030 |\n94: | SAC4C-P1-001 | 4c | P1 | Reproduced: `do not run /doctor:ci report or /create:readme` printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `db14c22bb0`, both doctor or-lists print no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:15-16`) | T031 |\n95: | SAC4C-P2-001 | 4c | P2 | Confirmed by reading: the phase 027 spec still called the question over an or-list out of scope | Fixed in the spec text, the scope line and A3 | Spec wording |\n96: | ARC4C-P2-001 | 4c | P2 | Rejected: `normalize` turns every redirect to a real file into a write, so the target never reaches `shellReadTargets` | T032 built, rejected by the Opus verifier and reverted | T032 declined |\n97: | ARC4C-P2-002 | 4c | P2 | Confirmed by reading the README against `command-offer.mjs` | Fixed in `db14c22bb0` | T033 |\n98: | ARC4C-P2-003 | 4c | P2 | Confirmed by reading the README against `command-offer.mjs` | Fixed in `db14c22bb0` | T033 |\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: ## 4. Convergence\n103: \n104: | Round | Lineage | Iterations | New-findings ratio per iteration | Stop reason |\n105: |-------|---------|------------|----------------------------------|-------------|\n106: | 1 | `scorer-attach-4` | 4 | 1, 1, 1, 1 | cap reached |\n107: | 1 | `render-hooks-plugin-4` | 4 | 1, 0.33, 0, 0 | converged |\n108: | 1 | `accuracy-runner-4` | 4 | 1, 1, 1, 1 | cap reached |\n109: | 1 | `doctor-docs-4` | 3 | 1, 0, 0 | cap reached |\n110: | 4b | `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` | 3 | 0.88, 0, 0 | cap reached |\n111: | 4b | `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b` | 3 | 0, 0, 1 | cap reached |\n112: | 4c | `scorer-attach-close-4c` | 3 | 1, 1, 0 | cap reached |\n113: | 4c | `accuracy-runner-close-4c` | 2 | 1, 0.6667 | cap reached |\n114: \n115: 26 iterations over the three rounds: 15 in round one and 11 in rounds 4b and 4c. The parent goal log row `Review pass four, confirming round` says 10 for rounds 4b and 4c, and the iteration records count 3, 3, 3 and 2. Two round-one lineages ended at 1.0 on their cap. Their findings went to the verifier, and rounds 4b and 4c read the fixes. The loop is closed on this judgment: the last round found one P1, which reproduced and is fixed, and README wording that is fixed or rejected, and the plan runs no round past 4c.\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## 5. Verification after the last fix\n120: \n121: At `db14c22bb0`, from phase 027 `scratch/after-3.txt`: the advisor suite reads 184 files and 2065 passed with 0 failed (2027 at BASE), the mention reader guards read 146 passed, the transcript scorer tests 172, the session reader tests 96 of 96, the history lookup tests 30 of 30, the doctor tests 1221 of 1221 and the plugin tests 45 of 45. The floors equal their before lines (`scratch/floor-after-3.txt`): typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, typed delivery 44 of 44, plain tune 28 of 45 and plain holdout 1 of 44. The fit counts read 8 and 0 and the scorer eval reads `[160,51,21,5]`. The mention probe prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`.\n122: \n123: ---\n124: \n125: ## 6. Audit Appendix\n126: \n127: - **Scope files:** `review/review-scope-4.txt` for round one, `review/review-scope-4b.txt` and `review/review-scope-4c.txt` for the two closing rounds.\n128: - **Fan-out configs:** `review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-4.json`, `-pass-4b.json` and `-pass-4c.json`.\n129: - **Briefs:** `review/review-brief-4.txt`, `-4b.txt` and `-4c.txt`.\n130: - **Lineage folders:** the eight folders above under `review/lineages/`, each with its own report, registry and state log.\n131: - **Verifier report and probes:** `review/verify-4/report.md` and `review/verify-4/probes/`.\n132: - **Adjudication of rounds 4b and 4c:** `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`.\n133: - **Merged registry:** `review/deep-review-findings-registry.json` and `review/fanout-attribution.md` were rewritten by the merge run of section 2 over all 22 lineages. This report, not that file, is the adjudicated record for pass four.\n134: - **Decision rows:** P044 to P051 in `decision-record.md`. P049 says the carry applies to the decline leads only and leaves a question over an or-list as it is. T029 later carried questions over an or-list too, after round 4b reproduced SAC4B-P2-001, so that clause of P049 no longer holds. The decision record was not edited in this pass.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md, lines 55-134\n55: \n56: ## 3. Verifier verdicts and outcome per finding\n57: \n58: Round one, from `review/verify-4/report.md`. The task column names the phase 027 task that fixed the finding, and the decision column names the row in `decision-record.md` for a finding that was not built.\n59: \n60: | Finding | Severity raised | Verifier verdict | Outcome | Task or decision |\n61: |---------|-----------------|------------------|---------|------------------|\n62: | SA4-P1-002 | P1 | Confirmed P1: a refusal over `A or B` keeps the second command | Fixed. The three or-list refusals now carry no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:2-4`) | T004 |\n63: | SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n64: | SA4-P1-003 | P1 | Confirmed, deliberate tradeoff, P2: broad creation words in a correction | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n65: | SA4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` keeps the command | Fixed. The question now carries no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:7`) | T005 |\n66: | SA4-P2-002 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `advisor-recommend.md:39` and the lead row's command | Fixed in the feature catalog page | T014 |\n67: | SA4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the meaning anchor test has 28 cases, not 17 | Fixed | T015 |\n68: | SA4-P2-004 | P2 | Confirmed P2: phase 020 says the weak-cue bar is 10, the code uses 9 | Closed by a superseding note in the phase 027 spec, phase 020 not edited | P048 |\n69: | SA4-P2-005 | P2 | Confirmed P2: no test row for the residual behaviours | Fixed by the rows T004 and T005 added | T004, T005 |\n70: | R4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the Codex reader opens the caller's path after containment resolved another | Fixed, the reader opens the resolved path (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:43`) | T010 |\n71: | R4-P2-002 | P2 | Rejected: the first returned row always leads | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n72: | R4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the advisor README should name `parent-named only` | Fixed | T016 |\n73: | iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | P1 | Confirmed P1: both run-log writers drop `offeredAs` | Fixed in both writers (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:39`) | T006, T007 |\n74: | iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated | P1 | Rejected: a move from 8 to 9 already fails the suite | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n75: | iter1-P2-heredoc-delimiter | P2 | Confirmed P2: an end word with `-` or `.` is read as a command | Fixed, every heredoc line reads `improvised` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:27-32`) | T008 |\n76: | iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start | P2 | Confirmed, raised to P1: a shell `cat` of a command document is not a start | Fixed, and every stored arm rescored (`scratch/rescore-delta.txt`) | T009, T021 |\n77: | iter2-P2-live-holdout-guard-baseline-only | P2 | Confirmed P2: the guard reads the committed baseline only | Fixed, the guard reads the live capture too | T011 |\n78: | iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned | P2 | Rejected: the slice test compares the whole block | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n79: | iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows | P2 | Confirmed P2: the paired block needs a shared owned row | Deferred to phase 026 task T030 | P046 |\n80: | iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision | P2 | Confirmed P2, hand-written logs only: reserve `paired` | Deferred to phase 026 task T053 | P046 |\n81: | iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field | P2 | Confirmed P2: delete the field | Deferred to phase 026 task T052 | P046 |\n82: | DR4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the A11 row should name the by-hand fix for a malformed row | Fixed | T017 |\n83: | The README statement, ungraded | not raised | Seen outside the 21, not graded: `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` heads `/create:readme (start)` | Recorded as a route vocabulary gap at P2, not fixed (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:8`) | P047 |\n84: \n85: Rounds 4b and 4c, adjudicated by the coordinator in `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/re