{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761568853,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0202ebc001rq0TdMXXxg7AUN","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e0200f9a001H5VuMTAo030TSo","type":"tool","id":"call_02a31bd7fa3f4ac8a9efb403","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"head -3 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-state.jsonl | cut -c1-1200; echo; echo \"=== iteration row\"; grep -m1 '\"type\":\"iteration\"' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-state.jsonl | cut -c1-3000"},"output":"{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"Review: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\",\"maxIterations\":4,\"generation\":1,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-14T15:29:09.038Z\"}\n{\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"dimensions\":[\"correctness\"],\"durationMs\":420000,\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-522\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:860-960,1120-1260,1580-1620\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:429-514,620-710\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-56,135-432\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:155-190,382-482\"],\"findingDetails\":[{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"typed-command attach\",\"retired-command map\",\"/create:sk-skill start policy\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The retired name could be treated as a distinct command, but the map's comment says it reads as the replacement, so the guards should agree.\",\"claim\":\"A refusal written with the retired command name still attaches the live command because the retired-name rewrite runs before the mention guard.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The compiled route for the same prompt returns defer, so the typed path is the live caller; the probe confirms the top row is sk-doc.\",\"downgradeTri\n{\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"dimensions\":[\"security\"],\"durationMs\":360000,\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:356-432\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1140-1231,1588-1618\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:311-364,429-488\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts:1-160\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:135-230\"],\"findingDetails\":[{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"doctor command rows\",\"question/statement phrasings\",\"/doctor:update ask policy\",\"hook brief third row\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The question is a yes/no safety question, not a request; the command offer would still ask before writing, so the impact is an unfit offer rather than a silent write.\",\"claim\":\"A question or statement that puts the noun 'command' between the ask word and the command name is not recognized by the mention reader, so the command row stays passing.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The direct form 'what does /doctor:update do?' withheld the row; the ask lead list allo\n\n=== iteration row\n{\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"dimensions\":[\"correctness\"],\"durationMs\":420000,\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-522\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:860-960,1120-1260,1580-1620\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:429-514,620-710\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-56,135-432\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:155-190,382-482\"],\"findingDetails\":[{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"typed-command attach\",\"retired-command map\",\"/create:sk-skill start policy\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The retired name could be treated as a distinct command, but the map's comment says it reads as the replacement, so the guards should agree.\",\"claim\":\"A refusal written with the retired command name still attaches the live command because the retired-name rewrite runs before the mention guard.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The compiled route for the same prompt returns defer, so the typed path is the live caller; the probe confirms the top row is sk-doc.\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if the retired name is deliberately excluded from the live command's refusal semantics.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:240\",\"command-attach.ts:256\",\"handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:500\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"findingClass\":\"guard_gap\",\"id\":\"SA4-P1-001\",\"iteration\":1,\"scopeProof\":\"command-attach.ts and handlers/advisor-recommend.ts are in the declared scorer-attach scope; the handler is the only production caller of typedCommandForTop.\",\"severity\":\"P1\",\"title\":\"A refusal typed with the retired command name still delivers the live mutating command\"},{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"typed-command attach\",\"multi-command refusals\",\"/deep:research ask policy\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The reader may have refused only the first command and merely named the second, but 'do not run A or B' refuses both.\",\"claim\":\"A refusal that coordinates two command names attaches the second one because the mention reader requires a separate lead before each occurrence.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterevidenceSought\":\"The compiled route returns defer and the scorer top is system-deep-loop; a single-command refusal is correctly withheld, so the gap is the coordinated form.\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade to P2 if a coordinated refusal is judged a mention of both commands rather than a refusal of both.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:414\",\"command-attach.ts:419\",\"command-attach.ts:360\"],\"file\":\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P1\",\"findingClass\":\"guard_gap\",\"id\":\"SA4-P1-002\",\"iteration\":1,\"scopeProof\":\"The prompt is an ordinary refusal of two tracked commands; the typed path and handler are in scope, and no other module rewrites the lead.\",\"s\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"Review: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\",\"maxIterations\":4,\"generation\":1,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-14T15:29:09.038Z\"}\n{\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"dimensions\":[\"correctness\"],\"durationMs\":420000,\"filesReviewed\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:1-522\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:860-960,1120-1260,1580-1620\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:429-514,620-710\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39-56,135-432\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts:155-190,382-482\"],\"findingDetails\":[{\"affectedSurfaceHints\":[\"typed-command attach\",\"retired-command map\",\"/create:sk-skill start policy\"],\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The retired name could be treated as a distinct command, but the map's comment says it reads as the replacement, so the guards should agree.\",\"claim\":\"A refusal written with the retired command name still attaches the live command because the retired-name rewrite runs before the mention guard.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"counterev