{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761678447,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"id":"prt_1e021de6f001SIj0koV4h6MkjC","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e021d022001Zl9ZryB39MzpdD","type":"step-start","snapshot":"8f0bd6eca7de83431aa7adb5210764f971212b0d"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761684655,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e021e6f2002cFHdJLKzQFfDMj","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e021d022001Zl9ZryB39MzpdD","type":"tool","id":"call_fb4706fe9bc0456fa774427a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the handler's real fallback shape instead of only the test's headed examples: the leading `\\nDirectives:` makes `indexOf` return 0, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command (iteration 1).\n- Reading `reduceRepeatedHead` first: its explicit `context.startsWith(label)` branch proves the authors know the fallback exists, which isolated the missing guard in `withCommandDocuments` rather than blaming the handler (iteration 1).\n- Walking the generated bridge table read-only: 69 of 69 `commandPolicies` rows resolve to a document, so the document-line mechanism is sound and the finding is the fallback boundary, not the resolution rule (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\n- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -86,15 +86,18 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the handler's real fallback shape instead of only the test's headed examples: the leading `\\nDirectives:` makes `indexOf` return 0, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command (iteration 1).\n+- Reading `reduceRepeatedHead` first: its explicit `context.startsWith(label)` branch proves the authors know the fallback exists, which isolated the missing guard in `withCommandDocuments` rather than blaming the handler (iteration 1).\n+- Walking the generated bridge table read-only: 69 of 69 `commandPolicies` rows resolve to a document, so the document-line mechanism is sound and the finding is the fallback boundary, not the resolution rule (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the handler's real fallback shape instead of only the test's headed examples: the leading `\\\\nDirectives:` makes `indexOf` return 0, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command (iteration 1).\\n- Reading `reduceRepeatedHead` first: its explicit `context.startsWith(label)` branch proves the authors know the fallback exists, which isolated the missing guard in `withCommandDocuments` rather than blaming the handler (iteration 1).\\n- Walking the generated bridge table read-only: 69 of 69 `commandPolicies` rows resolve to a document, so the document-line mechanism is sound and the finding is the fallback boundary, not the resolution rule (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761680626,"end":1794761684655}}}}
