{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761847565,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02461c0001Q8x1CK9XCH7JqM","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e02454e00014AkiJ14S69MQ2v","type":"tool","id":"call_8bb736f75acc49b59ce5cf29","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\n- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).","newString":"- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\n- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\n- Resolving the handler's `new URL('../../../../../../hooks/...', import.meta.url)` with node for both the source and the dist location: the source path lands one level above the repository while the dist path lands on `.skilled/hooks/shared`, which proves the canonical switch gap is source-only and keeps the finding at P2 (iteration 2).\n- Following the switch table row by row into the shared resolver and the plugin: both `_HOOK_DISABLED` and `_PLUGIN_DISABLED` sit in one alias list, and the plugin asks the same resolver, so the table's hook-versus-plugin distinction is not in the code (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9B. WHAT FAILED (continued)\n\n- Reading the source handler's switch check as proving the canonical switch failed: the resolver path is wrong from the source folder and the catch returns enabled. Only the explicit legacy-name check survives a source run (iteration 2).\n- Reading phase 029's `AC-009` as evidence for the alias rows failed: it verifies that the listed lines did not change, not that they are true (iteration 2)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -95,11 +95,20 @@\n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\n - Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\n+- Resolving the handler's `new URL('../../../../../../hooks/...', import.meta.url)` with node for both the source and the dist location: the source path lands one level above the repository while the dist path lands on `.skilled/hooks/shared`, which proves the canonical switch gap is source-only and keeps the finding at P2 (iteration 2).\n+- Following the switch table row by row into the shared resolver and the plugin: both `_HOOK_DISABLED` and `_PLUGIN_DISABLED` sit in one alias list, and the plugin asks the same resolver, so the table's hook-versus-plugin distinction is not in the code (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n+## 9B. WHAT FAILED (continued)\n+\n+- Reading the source handler's switch check as proving the canonical switch failed: the resolver path is wrong from the source folder and the catch returns enabled. Only the explicit legacy-name check survives a source run (iteration 2).\n+- Reading phase 029's `AC-009` as evidence for the alias rows failed: it verifies that the listed lines did not change, not that they are true (iteration 2).\n+\n+---\n+\n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### **The document line is added before the directive block.** Holds for a headed brief; fails only for the no-brief fallback above. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n - What was tried: **The document line is added before the directive block.** Holds for a headed brief; fails only for the no-brief fallback above.\n","status":"modified","additions":9,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\",\"newString\":\"- Reading the Vibe part's `env` injectable as covering every environment read failed: `headReceiptDir` reads `process.env` directly, so the child-marker test and the receipt path can disagree under injection. Recorded for the maintainability pass (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the subagent guard as proven failed: `parent_session_id` has no in-repo Vibe payload schema and no test, so the hook contract's subagent promise is a claim rather than a verified behavior (iteration 1).\\n- Resolving the handler's `new URL('../../../../../../hooks/...', import.meta.url)` with node for both the source and the dist location: the source path lands one level above the repository while the dist path lands on `.skilled/hooks/shared`, which proves the canonical switch gap is source-only and keeps the finding at P2 (iteration 2).\\n- Following the switch table row by row into the shared resolver and the plugin: both `_HOOK_DISABLED` and `_PLUGIN_DISABLED` sit in one alias list, and the plugin asks the same resolver, so the table's hook-versus-plugin distinction is not in the code (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9B. WHAT FAILED (continued)\\n\\n- Reading the source handler's switch check as proving the canonical switch failed: the resolver path is wrong from the source folder and the catch returns enabled. Only the explicit legacy-name check survives a source run (iteration 2).\\n- Reading phase 029's `AC-009` as evidence for the alias rows failed: it verifies that the listed lines did not change, not that they are true (iteration 2).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761843136,"end":1794761847565}}}}
