 completed-session | invalid-state\"\n462-          - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 of the state log bytes when resuming or restarting an existing lineage\"\n463-        lifecycle_routing:\n464-          - \"If lineage_mode == restart, step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so session_state is fresh and on_fresh runs.\"\n465-          - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n--\n587:          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n588-        on_invalid_state:\n589-          halt: true\n590-          release_lock: step_release_lock\n591-          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n592-        on_fresh:\n593-          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n594-\n595-      step_scope_discovery:\n596-        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n597-        resolve:\n598-          spec-folder: |\n599-            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n600-            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n601-            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n602-            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n603-            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n604-            6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n605-          skill: |\n606-            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n607-            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n608-            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n609-            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n610-            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n611-          agent: |\n612-            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n613-            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n614-            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n615-          track: |\n616-            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n617-            2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n618-            3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n619-          files: |\n620-            1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n621-            2. Validate all files exist\n622-            3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n623-            4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n624-        outputs:\n625-          - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n626-          - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n627-\n628-      step_order_dimensions:\n629-        action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n630-        algorithm: |\n631-          1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n632-          2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n633-             correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n634-          3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions\n635-          4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n636-             - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n637-             - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n638-          5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n639-          6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n640-        outputs:\n641-          - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n642-          - inventory_pass: true\n643-\n644-      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n645-        action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n646-        outputs:\n647-          - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n648-          - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n649-        normalize: |\n650-          Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n651-            - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n652-            - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n653-            - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n654-          Every element MUST be one of the four canonical dimension names.\n655-\n656-      step_normalize_review_focus:\n657-        action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n658-        outputs:\n659-          - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n660-        normalize: |\n661-          Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n662-          fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n663-\n664-      step_resolve_session_id:\n665-        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n666-        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n667-        if_present:\n668-          bind:\n669-            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n670-        if_absent:\n671-          bind:\n672-            session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n673-\n674-      step_create_config:\n675-        action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n676-        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n677-        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n678-        lineage_values:\n679-          generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n680-          lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n681-          parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n682-        populate:\n683-          topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n684-          mode: \"review\"\n685-          sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n686-          parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n687-          lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n688-          generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n689-          continuedFromRun: null\n690-          reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n691-          reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n692-          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n693-          reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n694-          # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n695-          reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n696-          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n697-          reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n698-          severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n699-          crossReference:\n700-            core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n701-            overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n702-          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status