{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762156257,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0291bc3001E8EU7NJ0ZudL31","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e028f83d001PxDIu5CKahZZzm","type":"tool","id":"call_7175c179085e4d1c92b18515","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Reading the hook contract's per-runtime section as complete after the Vibe row failed: the section intro and the \"starting a surfaced command\" table still enumerate the older runtimes only (iteration 3).\n- Reading the Vibe part's dependency object as fully injectable failed: `env` reaches only the child-session test while the receipt directory keeps reading the process environment, so a caller that injects only `env` writes to the real temporary folder (iteration 4).\n- Reading the doctor contract test as covering the Vibe rows by name failed: the route case is still titled for DSH while the array it walks holds both runtimes (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9D. WHAT WORKED (continued)\n\n- Reading the suite's injected `read`/`write` pair against the module's default pair: the suite is hermetic, which isolates the gap to the documented `env` dependency rather than to the tests (iteration 4).\n- Reading `MIRROR_CHECKS` and the two gap walks before judging the test name: the coverage is complete and only the title is stale, so the finding stays a naming gap instead of a coverage claim (iteration 4).","oldString":"- Reading the hook contract's per-runtime section as complete after the Vibe row failed: the section intro and the \"starting a surfaced command\" table still enumerate the older runtimes only (iteration 3).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -106,11 +106,20 @@\n - Reading the source handler's switch check as proving the canonical switch failed: the resolver path is wrong from the source folder and the catch returns enabled. Only the explicit legacy-name check survives a source run (iteration 2).\n - Reading phase 029's `AC-009` as evidence for the alias rows failed: it verifies that the listed lines did not change, not that they are true (iteration 2).\n - Reading the Vibe reader as covering every field the host acts on failed: it reads only `type` and `command`, so a `match` filter is invisible even though the repository's own hooks file uses `match` values, including `agents_spawn` (iteration 3).\n - Reading the hook contract's per-runtime section as complete after the Vibe row failed: the section intro and the \"starting a surfaced command\" table still enumerate the older runtimes only (iteration 3).\n+- Reading the Vibe part's dependency object as fully injectable failed: `env` reaches only the child-session test while the receipt directory keeps reading the process environment, so a caller that injects only `env` writes to the real temporary folder (iteration 4).\n+- Reading the doctor contract test as covering the Vibe rows by name failed: the route case is still titled for DSH while the array it walks holds both runtimes (iteration 4).\n \n ---\n \n+## 9D. WHAT WORKED (continued)\n+\n+- Reading the suite's injected `read`/`write` pair against the module's default pair: the suite is hermetic, which isolates the gap to the documented `env` dependency rather than to the tests (iteration 4).\n+- Reading `MIRROR_CHECKS` and the two gap walks before judging the test name: the coverage is complete and only the title is stale, so the finding stays a naming gap instead of a coverage claim (iteration 4).\n+\n+---\n+\n ## 9C. WHAT WORKED (continued)\n \n - Running the wiring check on this checkout before judging it: five `ok` lines and exit 0 prove the real `.vibe/hooks.toml` parses through the line reader, so the finding is the ignored `match` field rather than the reader (iteration 3).\n - Counting the three Vibe script names in the workflow and the route instead of trusting the comment: nine and three lines match the contract test's assertions and phase 030's `REQ-005` (iteration 3).\n","status":"modified","additions":9,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Reading the hook contract's per-runtime section as complete after the Vibe row failed: the section intro and the \\\"starting a surfaced command\\\" table still enumerate the older runtimes only (iteration 3).\\n- Reading the Vibe part's dependency object as fully injectable failed: `env` reaches only the child-session test while the receipt directory keeps reading the process environment, so a caller that injects only `env` writes to the real temporary folder (iteration 4).\\n- Reading the doctor contract test as covering the Vibe rows by name failed: the route case is still titled for DSH while the array it walks holds both runtimes (iteration 4).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9D. WHAT WORKED (continued)\\n\\n- Reading the suite's injected `read`/`write` pair against the module's default pair: the suite is hermetic, which isolates the gap to the documented `env` dependency rather than to the tests (iteration 4).\\n- Reading `MIRROR_CHECKS` and the two gap walks before judging the test name: the coverage is complete and only the title is stale, so the finding stays a naming gap instead of a coverage claim (iteration 4).\",\"oldString\":\"- Reading the hook contract's per-runtime section as complete after the Vibe row failed: the section intro and the \\\"starting a surfaced command\\\" table still enumerate the older runtimes only (iteration 3).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794762152899,"end":1794762156257}}}}
