{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762197023,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e029c0fc001v2HgRHrtP0KnNE","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e029a908001a1laL1zF83T76G","type":"tool","id":"call_92616b42b21a4811aa9b5019","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst d=\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/\";\nconst reg=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(d+\"deep-review-findings-registry.json\",\"utf8\"));\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({counts:reg.findingsBySeverity,open:reg.openFindingsCount,resolved:reg.resolvedFindingsCount,coverage:reg.dimensionCoverage,convergence:reg.convergenceScore,divergence:reg.divergence,terminalGates:reg.terminalGates},null,1).slice(0,1800));\nconsole.log(\"FINDINGS\");\nfor(const f of reg.openFindings) console.log([f.findingId,f.severity,f.dimensions?f.dimensions.join(\"+\"):\"\",f.file||f.location,f.title].join(\" | \"));\n'"},"output":"{\n \"counts\": {\n  \"P0\": 0,\n  \"P1\": 0,\n  \"P2\": 8\n },\n \"open\": 8,\n \"resolved\": 0,\n \"coverage\": {\n  \"correctness\": true,\n  \"security\": true,\n  \"traceability\": true,\n  \"maintainability\": true\n },\n \"convergence\": 0.75,\n \"divergence\": {\n  \"started\": [],\n  \"completed\": [],\n  \"failed\": [],\n  \"overrides\": [],\n  \"saturatedDirections\": [],\n  \"remainingFrontier\": [],\n  \"currentFocus\": \"\"\n },\n \"terminalGates\": null\n}\nFINDINGS\nR1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs | The no-brief fallback is read as a routing head, so a command named in the directive block gains a document line after the directives\nR1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs | The subagent guard keys on a field no Vibe source or test names, while the hook contract promises a subagent turn gets no brief\nR2-P2-001 | P2 | security | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts | The handler resolves the shared switch resolver one level above the repository when it runs from source, so the canonical kill switch fails open there\nR2-P2-002 | P2 | security | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | The switch table implies a hook-versus-plugin split that the shared resolver does not make, so either name silences every adapter\nR3-P2-001 | P2 | traceability | .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs | The Vibe row ignores the hook match filter, so an entry Vibe never runs on a main turn still reads ok vibe\nR3-P2-002 | P2 | traceability | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md | The hook contract names Vibe in its per-runtime table but leaves it out of the two runtime summaries that table feeds\nR4-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs | The dependency object env does not reach the receipt path, so a caller that injects only env still writes to and reads from the real temporary folder\nR4-P2-002 | P2 | maintainability | .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs | The doctor contract test name says it checks DSH only while it now asserts the Vibe rows too\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"counts\": {\n  \"P0\": 0,\n  \"P1\": 0,\n  \"P2\": 8\n },\n \"open\": 8,\n \"resolved\": 0,\n \"coverage\": {\n  \"correctness\": true,\n  \"security\": true,\n  \"traceability\": true,\n  \"maintainability\": true\n },\n \"convergence\": 0.75,\n \"divergence\": {\n  \"started\": [],\n  \"completed\": [],\n  \"failed\": [],\n  \"overrides\": [],\n  \"saturatedDirections\": [],\n  \"remainingFrontier\": [],\n  \"currentFocus\": \"\"\n },\n \"terminalGates\": null\n}\nFINDINGS\nR1-P2-00