{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762483202,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02e0730002oPNQlrhEW7yNWS","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e02ddfce001Ey2Ck8dcsPl4bi","type":"tool","id":"call_9792ed6255894bcc9bf60f4f","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"1. **A context that starts with the directive block is read as a routing head, so a command named in that older-build fallback gains a document line after the directives** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` -- `withCommandDocuments` splits the context at `context.indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` and treats a split at index 0 or a miss as \"no directive block\" (`separator > 0`). A context that begins with `Directives:` — the directive-only fallback an older advisor build rendered, which `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly recognizes at `:176-177` — is therefore scanned as a head, and a command named inside that directive text gains a `Command documents ...` line appended after the directives. The current handler always renders a status head before the directives, so this input is the older-build shape the module still supports, not today's fallback.\n   Finding class: boundary_parsing\n   Scope proof: The Vibe part is a declared `vibe-hooks-doctor` file; `withCommandDocuments` is its only document-line producer, and the directive-only shape it mis-reads is named by its sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` in the same file.\n   Affected surface hints: Vibe directive-only fallback, document line placement, directive block.\n   Case: With the directive-only context `Directives:\\n- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.`, the part returns that text plus `\\nCommand documents (read in full before taking one): /speckit:save is .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md.` `reduceRepeatedHead` returns the same input unchanged, so the two functions disagree about the same shape. The current headed fallback `Advisor: no skill matched.\\nDirectives:\\n- ...` is unchanged by `withCommandDocuments`, as the probe also showed.\n   Evidence: `prompt-advisor.mjs:125-127` (`separator > 0`), `prompt-advisor.mjs:174-177` (the sibling branch that recognizes `Directives:` at the start), and the module probe recorded in this iteration's probe output.","oldString":"1. **The no-brief fallback is read as a routing head, so a command named in the directive block gains a document line after the directives** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` -- `withCommandDocuments` splits the context at `context.indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` and treats a separator at index 0 as \"no directive block\" (`separator > 0`). The handler's no-brief fallback begins with exactly `\\nDirectives:`, so the fallback is scanned as a head and a command named inside the directive text gains a `Command documents ...` line appended after the directives, though the advisor offered no command.\n   Finding class: boundary_parsing\n   Scope proof: The Vibe part is a declared `vibe-hooks-doctor` file; `withCommandDocuments` is its only document-line producer, and the fallback shape it mis-reads is produced by the in-scope handler at `user-prompt-submit.ts:373` and pinned by the fallback constant at `claude-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts:37`.\n   Affected surface hints: Vibe no-brief fallback, document line placement, directive block.\n   Case: With a directive block holding `- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.` and the prompt `summarize this module` (no match, so the handler returns the fallback), the part returns `\\nDirectives:\\n- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.\\nCommand documents (read in full before taking one): /speckit:save is .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md.` The probe was run against the module's exported `withCommandDocuments`; the same call with a bare `Advisor: no skill matched.` head is unchanged.\n   Evidence: `prompt-advisor.mjs:125-127` (`separator > 0`), `prompt-advisor.mjs:176-177` (the sibling branch that does recognize a context starting with the label), and `user-prompt-submit.ts:373`.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md\n@@ -27,14 +27,14 @@\n None.\n \n ### P2 Findings\n \n-1. **The no-brief fallback is read as a routing head, so a command named in the directive block gains a document line after the directives** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` -- `withCommandDocuments` splits the context at `context.indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` and treats a separator at index 0 as \"no directive block\" (`separator > 0`). The handler's no-brief fallback begins with exactly `\\nDirectives:`, so the fallback is scanned as a head and a command named inside the directive text gains a `Command documents ...` line appended after the directives, though the advisor offered no command.\n+1. **A context that starts with the directive block is read as a routing head, so a command named in that older-build fallback gains a document line after the directives** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` -- `withCommandDocuments` splits the context at `context.indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` and treats a split at index 0 or a miss as \"no directive block\" (`separator > 0`). A context that begins with `Directives:` — the directive-only fallback an older advisor build rendered, which `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly recognizes at `:176-177` — is therefore scanned as a head, and a command named inside that directive text gains a `Command documents ...` line appended after the directives. The current handler always renders a status head before the directives, so this input is the older-build shape the module still supports, not today's fallback.\n    Finding class: boundary_parsing\n-   Scope proof: The Vibe part is a declared `vibe-hooks-doctor` file; `withCommandDocuments` is its only document-line producer, and the fallback shape it mis-reads is produced by the in-scope handler at `user-prompt-submit.ts:373` and pinned by the fallback constant at `claude-user-prompt-submit-hook.vitest.ts:37`.\n-   Affected surface hints: Vibe no-brief fallback, document line placement, directive block.\n-   Case: With a directive block holding `- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.` and the prompt `summarize this module` (no match, so the handler returns the fallback), the part returns `\\nDirectives:\\n- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.\\nCommand documents (read in full before taking one): /speckit:save is .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md.` The probe was run against the module's exported `withCommandDocuments`; the same call with a bare `Advisor: no skill matched.` head is unchanged.\n-   Evidence: `prompt-advisor.mjs:125-127` (`separator > 0`), `prompt-advisor.mjs:176-177` (the sibling branch that does recognize a context starting with the label), and `user-prompt-submit.ts:373`.\n+   Scope proof: The Vibe part is a declared `vibe-hooks-doctor` file; `withCommandDocuments` is its only document-line producer, and the directive-only shape it mis-reads is named by its sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` in the same file.\n+   Affected surface hints: Vibe directive-only fallback, document line placement, directive block.\n+   Case: With the directive-only context `Directives:\\n- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.`, the part returns that text plus `\\nCommand documents (read in full before taking one): /speckit:save is .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md.` `reduceRepeatedHead` returns the same input unchanged, so the two functions disagree about the same shape. The current headed fallback `Advisor: no skill matched.\\nDirectives:\\n- ...` is unchanged by `withCommandDocuments`, as the probe also showed.\n+   Evidence: `prompt-advisor.mjs:125-127` (`separator > 0`), `prompt-advisor.mjs:174-177` (the sibling branch that recognizes `Directives:` at the start), and the module probe recorded in this iteration's probe output.\n \n 2. **The subagent guard keys on a payload field no Vibe source or test names, while the hook contract promises a subagent turn gets no brief** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:64` -- `isChildSession` treats a non-empty `payload.parent_session_id` as the subagent marker. No file in the repository defines a Vibe `pre_agent` payload schema or names that key, and the Vibe suite has no case that sets it, so the doc's promise at `skill-advisor-hook.md:95` rests on an unproven field name.\n    Finding class: unverified_claim\n    Scope proof: Both files are in the declared scope; the only other child marker is `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, which the manual scenario covers and which is a different, proven path.\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":5}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-001.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"1. **A context that starts with the directive block is read as a routing head, so a command named in that older-build fallback gains a document line after the directives** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` -- `withCommandDocuments` splits the context at `context.indexOf('\\\\nDirectives:')` and treats a split at index 0 or a miss as \\\"no directive block\\\" (`separator > 0`). A context that begins with `Directives:` — the directive-only fallback an older advisor build rendered, which `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly recognizes at `:176-177` — is therefore scanned as a head, and a command named inside that directive text gains a `Command documents ...` line appended after the directives. The current handler always renders a status head before the directives, so this input is the older-build shape the module still supports, not today's fallback.\\n   Finding class: boundary_parsing\\n   Scope proof: The Vibe part is a declared `vibe-hooks-doctor` file; `withCommandDocuments` is its only document-line producer, and the directive-only shape it mis-reads is named by its sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` in the same file.\\n   Affected surface hints: Vibe directive-only fallback, document line placement, directive block.\\n   Case: With the directive-only context `Directives:\\\\n- When a save is due, run /speckit:save to record the session.`, the part returns that text plus `\\\\nCommand documents (read in full before taking one): /speckit:save is .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md.` `reduceRepeatedHead` returns the same input unchanged, so the two functions disagree about the same shape. The current headed fallback `Advisor: no skill matched.\\\\nDirectives:\\\\n- ...` is unchanged by `withCommandDocuments`, as the probe also showed