{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762507489,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02e7d90001xlTS01FacmHmzO","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e02e65ee001GN7I0MQOl2KrFJ","type":"tool","id":"call_c41f2aa80790416ea96958e0","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the directive-only context the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly supports: `Directives:` at the start makes `indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` miss, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command, while the same probe of the current headed fallback was unchanged (iteration 1).","oldString":"- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the handler's real fallback shape instead of only the test's headed examples: the leading `\\nDirectives:` makes `indexOf` return 0, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -86,9 +86,9 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the handler's real fallback shape instead of only the test's headed examples: the leading `\\nDirectives:` makes `indexOf` return 0, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command (iteration 1).\n+- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the directive-only context the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly supports: `Directives:` at the start makes `indexOf('\\nDirectives:')` miss, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command, while the same probe of the current headed fallback was unchanged (iteration 1).\n - Reading `reduceRepeatedHead` first: its explicit `context.startsWith(label)` branch proves the authors know the fallback exists, which isolated the missing guard in `withCommandDocuments` rather than blaming the handler (iteration 1).\n - Walking the generated bridge table read-only: 69 of 69 `commandPolicies` rows resolve to a document, so the document-line mechanism is sound and the finding is the fallback boundary, not the resolution rule (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the directive-only context the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` explicitly supports: `Directives:` at the start makes `indexOf('\\\\nDirectives:')` miss, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command, while the same probe of the current headed fallback was unchanged (iteration 1).\",\"oldString\":\"- Probing the exported `withCommandDocuments` with the handler's real fallback shape instead of only the test's headed examples: the leading `\\\\nDirectives:` makes `indexOf` return 0, so the `separator > 0` guard fails and the directive text is scanned as a head. The probe printed the extra line with a directive that names a command (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794762505616,"end":1794762507489}}}}
