{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762515452,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02e993f002yr0PPdTtKq0yDr","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e02e8aaf001WX4ldvbMU1u8QX","type":"tool","id":"call_ae78768c264d490fae06caa3","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- **What the focus checks found:** the kill switch and the direct-call off switch stop every shipped path (Vibe, Pi, DSH, Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, the OpenCode plugin and the direct call), with one source-run resolver gap recorded as P2. The doctor reads `.vibe/hooks.toml` correctly for the entry it claims to check, but ignores the `match` filter, which is P2. The Vibe document line is produced only for a real head, except for a context that begins with the directive block (the older-build no-head shape), which can gain a document line for a command named in its directives. Docs and code disagree in two places: the switch table's alias scope and the hook contract's runtime summaries.","oldString":"- **What the focus checks found:** the kill switch and the direct-call off switch stop every shipped path (Vibe, Pi, DSH, Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, the OpenCode plugin and the direct call), with one source-run resolver gap recorded as P2. The doctor reads `.vibe/hooks.toml` correctly for the entry it claims to check, but ignores the `match` filter, which is P2. The Vibe document line is produced only for a real head except when the no-brief fallback carries a command in its directives, which is P2. Docs and code disagree in two places: the switch table's alias scope and the hook contract's runtime summaries.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n@@ -16,9 +16,9 @@\n - **hasAdvisories: true.** Eight active P2 findings are recorded; none is a blocker.\n - **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 0, P2 8.\n - **Review scope summary:** the Vibe prompt-advisor part (new this pass), the Claude handler line that labels runtime observations, the doctor hook-wiring check's Vibe row and line reader, the runtime-mirrors route and CI rows, the command-reference allowlist, the hook contract's Vibe and switch sections, and the doctor contract test.\n - **Operator review focus:** Code review pass five of command surfacing. Read review/review-brief-5.txt in the packet first and follow it. Review the files in review/review-scope-5.txt whose area equals your lineage label without its -5 suffix, plus docs that describe them. Each finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input. Check the kill switch and direct-call switch paths, command offers on refusal, question, history or mention, Vibe journal scoring, the doctor hooks-file reading, docs against code, and holdout hygiene. Never open command-prompts.jsonl, holdout-prompts.jsonl or behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl except through jq del(.prompt), and print counts only. Change no code and write only inside your lineage folder.\n-- **What the focus checks found:** the kill switch and the direct-call off switch stop every shipped path (Vibe, Pi, DSH, Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, the OpenCode plugin and the direct call), with one source-run resolver gap recorded as P2. The doctor reads `.vibe/hooks.toml` correctly for the entry it claims to check, but ignores the `match` filter, which is P2. The Vibe document line is produced only for a real head except when the no-brief fallback carries a command in its directives, which is P2. Docs and code disagree in two places: the switch table's alias scope and the hook contract's runtime summaries.\n+- **What the focus checks found:** the kill switch and the direct-call off switch stop every shipped path (Vibe, Pi, DSH, Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, the OpenCode plugin and the direct call), with one source-run resolver gap recorded as P2. The doctor reads `.vibe/hooks.toml` correctly for the entry it claims to check, but ignores the `match` filter, which is P2. The Vibe document line is produced only for a real head, except for a context that begins with the directive block (the older-build no-head shape), which can gain a document line for a command named in its directives. Docs and code disagree in two places: the switch table's alias scope and the hook contract's runtime summaries.\n - **Command offers on refusal, question, history or mention:** the attach and mention guards are the `scorer-attach` area and this lineage did not re-review them. It checked the one Vibe surface that can still surface a command (the document line) and found the fallback case above.\n - **Vibe journal scoring:** the transcript scorer is the `accuracy-runner-5` area. This lineage read no scorer code and no journal row; the boundary is recorded in Deferred Items.\n - **Holdout:** no scoped file names `command-prompts.jsonl`, `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or `behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl`; no corpus file was opened and no prompt text was printed.\n - **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached without a convergence event, per the release-readiness rule that only a converged PASS or CONDITIONAL becomes `converged`.\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- **What the focus checks found:** the kill switch and the direct-call off switch stop every shipped path (Vibe, Pi, DSH, Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, the OpenCode plugin and the direct call), with one source-run resolver gap recorded as P2. The doctor reads `.vibe/hooks.toml` correctly for the entry it claims to check, but ignores the `match` filter, which is P2. The Vibe document line is produced only for a real head, except for a context that begins with the directive block (the older-build no-head shape), which can gain a document line for a command named in its directives. Docs and code disagree in two places: the switch table's alias scope and the hook contract's runtime summaries.\",\"oldString\":\"- **What the focus checks found:** the kill switch and the direct-call off switch stop every shipped path (Vibe, Pi, DSH, Claude, Codex, Cursor, Devin, the OpenCode plugin and the direct call), with one source-run resolver gap recorded as P2. The doctor reads `.vibe/hooks.toml` correctly for the entry it claims to check, but ignores the `match` filter, which is P2. The Vibe document line is produced only for a real head except when the no-brief fallback carries a command in its directives, which is P2. Docs and code disagree in two places: the switch table's alias scope and the hook contract's runtime summaries.\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794762512703,"end":1794762515452}}}}
