{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762523748,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02eb61f002g28PtpZrx1DbsE","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e02eaa040011qdRdh8m741MsW","type":"tool","id":"call_38135e1404e9470db1759c5f","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` | `separator > 0` treats a context that starts with the directive block as a head; `reduceRepeatedHead:174-177` explicitly recognizes the directive-only older-build shape, and the probe shows `withCommandDocuments` appends a document line to it. The current headed fallback `Advisor: ...\\nDirectives:` is unchanged. | A directive-only fallback whose directive text names a command gains a `Command documents` line after the directives, though no command was offered. | Treat a context that starts with `Directives:` as headless and return it unchanged, mirroring `reduceRepeatedHead`. | Advisory | `boundary_parsing` | The part is in scope; the directive-only shape is documented by its sibling function. | Vibe directive-only fallback, document line placement |","oldString":"| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` | `separator > 0` treats a context starting with `\\nDirectives:` as a head; the handler's fallback has exactly that shape (`user-prompt-submit.ts:373`), and the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` has the leading-label branch this function lacks (`:176-177`). | A no-brief fallback whose directive text names a command gains a `Command documents` line after the directives, though no command was offered. | Split on `>= 0` and return the context unchanged when the separator is at index 0, mirroring `reduceRepeatedHead`. | Advisory | `boundary_parsing` | The part is in scope; the fallback shape comes from the in-scope handler. | Vibe no-brief fallback, document line placement |","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n@@ -67,9 +67,9 @@\n ## 3. Active Finding Registry\n \n | ID | Sev | Dimension | Location | Evidence | Impact | Fix recommendation | Disposition | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surfaces |\n |----|-----|-----------|----------|----------|--------|--------------------|-------------|---------------|-------------|-------------------|\n-| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` | `separator > 0` treats a context starting with `\\nDirectives:` as a head; the handler's fallback has exactly that shape (`user-prompt-submit.ts:373`), and the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` has the leading-label branch this function lacks (`:176-177`). | A no-brief fallback whose directive text names a command gains a `Command documents` line after the directives, though no command was offered. | Split on `>= 0` and return the context unchanged when the separator is at index 0, mirroring `reduceRepeatedHead`. | Advisory | `boundary_parsing` | The part is in scope; the fallback shape comes from the in-scope handler. | Vibe no-brief fallback, document line placement |\n+| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` | `separator > 0` treats a context that starts with the directive block as a head; `reduceRepeatedHead:174-177` explicitly recognizes the directive-only older-build shape, and the probe shows `withCommandDocuments` appends a document line to it. The current headed fallback `Advisor: ...\\nDirectives:` is unchanged. | A directive-only fallback whose directive text names a command gains a `Command documents` line after the directives, though no command was offered. | Treat a context that starts with `Directives:` as headless and return it unchanged, mirroring `reduceRepeatedHead`. | Advisory | `boundary_parsing` | The part is in scope; the directive-only shape is documented by its sibling function. | Vibe directive-only fallback, document line placement |\n | R1-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:64` | `isChildSession` reads `payload.parent_session_id`; no Vibe payload schema in the repository names the key and the Vibe suite has no case for it (`vibe-prompt-advisor.vitest.ts`). | The contract's \"a subagent turn gets no brief\" is unverified; a payload that marks its parent under another key gets a brief. | Cite Vibe's payload contract and add a case, or soften `skill-advisor-hook.md:95`. | Advisory | `unverified_claim` | Part and contract are in scope; `AI_SESSION_CHILD` is the only proven child marker. | Vibe subagent turns, child-session suppression |\n | R2-P2-001 | P2 | security | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:71` | Six parent hops from the source folder resolve `<repository-parent>/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`; the `require` throws and `skillAdvisorHookEnabled` returns `true`. The dist file resolves `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`. | A source-run handler ignores `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`; only the explicit `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED === '1'` check at `:301` stops it. | Resolve the resolver by walking up to the nearest `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs`, as `advisor-disabled.ts` does. | Advisory | `fail_open_control_bypass` | The handler is in scope; the shipped dist path resolves. | Canonical kill switch, source-run handler |\n | R2-P2-002 | P2 | security | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:173` | `hook-flags.cjs:70-77` lists both `_HOOK_DISABLED` and `_PLUGIN_DISABLED` as aliases of one concern; the OpenCode plugin asks the same resolver at `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:205-207`, as does the Vibe part at `prompt-advisor.mjs:216`. | The table implies a hook-versus-plugin split; either name silences every adapter. | State that both names disable every adapter, or give the two names distinct resolvers. | Advisory | `doc_code_drift` | The contract is in scope; the resolver and plugin are context evidence. | Kill-switch documentation, OpenCode plugin, Vibe part |\n | R3-P2-001 | P2 | traceability | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` | `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command`; `match` is ignored. The repository's `.vibe/hooks.toml` uses `match` on this event family, including `agents_spawn` at `:84`. | An entry with `match = \"agents_spawn\"` reads `ok vibe` although turn-start never runs for the main agent. | Read `match` and require the main-agent form (or no filter) before reporting the entry wired. | Advisory | `false_pass_diagnostic` | The check and test are in scope; the hooks file is the input it reads. | Doctor hook-wiring check, Vibe prompt entry |\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` | `separator > 0` treats a context that starts with the directive block as a head; `reduceRepeatedHead:174-177` explicitly recognizes the directive-only older-build shape, and the probe shows `withCommandDocuments` appends a document line to it. The current headed fallback `Advisor: ...\\\\nDirectives:` is unchanged. | A directive-only fallback whose directive text names a command gains a `Command documents` line after the directives, though no command was offered. | Treat a context that starts with `Directives:` as headless and return it unchanged, mirroring `reduceRepeatedHead`. | Advisory | `boundary_parsing` | The part is in scope; the directive-only shape is documented by its sibling function. | Vibe directive-only fallback, document line placement |\",\"oldString\":\"| R1-P2-001 | P2 | correctness | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/vibe/prompt-advisor.mjs:125` | `separator > 0` treats a context starting with `\\\\nDirectives:` as a head; the handler's fallback has exactly that shape (`user-prompt-submit.ts:373`), and the sibling `reduceRepeatedHead` has the leading-label branch this function lacks (`:176-177`). | A no-brief fallback whose directive text names a command gains a `Command documents` line after the directives, though no command was offered. | Split on `>= 0` and return the context unchanged when the separator is at index 0, mirroring `reduceRepeatedHead`. | Advisory | `boundary_parsing` | The part is in scope; the fallback shape comes from the in-scope handler. | Vibe no-brief fallback, document line placement |\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794762520095,"end":1794762523748}}}}
