{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762583527,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02f92c0002yyyhovZA8DY7OI","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e02f6e25001g5UtbxXCLiyZOA","type":"tool","id":"call_99ebac7122bb41aa944df36e","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"1. **The Vibe row ignores the hook's `match` filter, so an entry scoped away from the main agent still reads `ok vibe`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` -- `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command` from each `[[hooks]]` block, and `inspect` accepts a block whose type is `pre_agent` and whose command ends with the marker. Vibe's own file pairs `match = \"main\"` with its turn-start and turn-end hooks, which is the evidence that the field scopes the hook to the main agent; the check never reads it.\n   Finding class: false_pass_diagnostic\n   Scope proof: The check and its test are declared scope files; the `.vibe/hooks.toml` field values and the README claim are read to test whether the check reports what it says it reports.\n   Affected surface hints: doctor hook-wiring check, Vibe prompt entry, target-repository diagnostics.\n   Case: A `.vibe/hooks.toml` block with `type = \"pre_agent\"`, a `match` value other than the main-agent form (the file already uses `agents_spawn`, `re:write_file|edit` and `ask_user_question` on other hooks) and the turn-start command prints `ok vibe` and exits 0, while the main prompt gets no turn-start. The filter semantics are an inference from the tracked file's pairing of `match = \"main\"` with both turn hooks; the check's own contract is that it never reads the field.\n   Evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` (the `type|command` regex), `:253-255` (the filter), `:350-361` (the toml branch), `.vibe/hooks.toml:18` and `:28` (`match = \"main\"` on the turn hooks) against `:84`, `:92` and `:135` (other match values), `README.markdown:112` (the claim that the check reports whether the prompt entry is wired).","oldString":"1. **The Vibe row ignores the hook's `match` filter, so an entry Vibe never runs on a main turn still reads `ok vibe`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` -- `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command` from each `[[hooks]]` block, and `inspect` accepts a block whose type is `pre_agent` and whose command ends with the marker. Vibe's own file proves `match` is a real filter on this event family, and a `match` value other than `main` means turn-start does not run for the main agent.\n   Finding class: false_pass_diagnostic\n   Scope proof: The check and its test are declared scope files; the `.vibe/hooks.toml` field values and the README claim are read to test whether the check reports what it says it reports.\n   Affected surface hints: doctor hook-wiring check, Vibe prompt entry, target-repository diagnostics.\n   Case: A `.vibe/hooks.toml` block with `type = \"pre_agent\"`, `match = \"agents_spawn\"` and `command = \"node \\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs\\\"\"` prints `ok vibe` and exits 0, while Vibe launches turn-start only for the agents-spawn event and the main prompt gets no brief.\n   Evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` (the `type|command` regex), `:253-255` (the filter), `:350-361` (the toml branch), `.vibe/hooks.toml:18` (`match = \"main\"` on turn-start) and `:84` (`match = \"agents_spawn\"` on another hook), `README.markdown:112` (the claim that the check reports whether the prompt entry is wired).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md\n@@ -31,14 +31,14 @@\n None.\n \n ### P2 Findings\n \n-1. **The Vibe row ignores the hook's `match` filter, so an entry Vibe never runs on a main turn still reads `ok vibe`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` -- `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command` from each `[[hooks]]` block, and `inspect` accepts a block whose type is `pre_agent` and whose command ends with the marker. Vibe's own file proves `match` is a real filter on this event family, and a `match` value other than `main` means turn-start does not run for the main agent.\n+1. **The Vibe row ignores the hook's `match` filter, so an entry scoped away from the main agent still reads `ok vibe`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` -- `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command` from each `[[hooks]]` block, and `inspect` accepts a block whose type is `pre_agent` and whose command ends with the marker. Vibe's own file pairs `match = \"main\"` with its turn-start and turn-end hooks, which is the evidence that the field scopes the hook to the main agent; the check never reads it.\n    Finding class: false_pass_diagnostic\n    Scope proof: The check and its test are declared scope files; the `.vibe/hooks.toml` field values and the README claim are read to test whether the check reports what it says it reports.\n    Affected surface hints: doctor hook-wiring check, Vibe prompt entry, target-repository diagnostics.\n-   Case: A `.vibe/hooks.toml` block with `type = \"pre_agent\"`, `match = \"agents_spawn\"` and `command = \"node \\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs\\\"\"` prints `ok vibe` and exits 0, while Vibe launches turn-start only for the agents-spawn event and the main prompt gets no brief.\n-   Evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` (the `type|command` regex), `:253-255` (the filter), `:350-361` (the toml branch), `.vibe/hooks.toml:18` (`match = \"main\"` on turn-start) and `:84` (`match = \"agents_spawn\"` on another hook), `README.markdown:112` (the claim that the check reports whether the prompt entry is wired).\n+   Case: A `.vibe/hooks.toml` block with `type = \"pre_agent\"`, a `match` value other than the main-agent form (the file already uses `agents_spawn`, `re:write_file|edit` and `ask_user_question` on other hooks) and the turn-start command prints `ok vibe` and exits 0, while the main prompt gets no turn-start. The filter semantics are an inference from the tracked file's pairing of `match = \"main\"` with both turn hooks; the check's own contract is that it never reads the field.\n+   Evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` (the `type|command` regex), `:253-255` (the filter), `:350-361` (the toml branch), `.vibe/hooks.toml:18` and `:28` (`match = \"main\"` on the turn hooks) against `:84`, `:92` and `:135` (other match values), `README.markdown:112` (the claim that the check reports whether the prompt entry is wired).\n \n 2. **The hook contract names Vibe in its per-runtime table but leaves it out of the two runtime summaries that table feeds** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:84` -- The section opens \"Every native runtime, Pi and DSH run the same hook handler\", which omits the Vibe part that the new row at line 95 says proxies the compiled handler; the \"Starting a surfaced command\" table at lines 103-111 has rows for seven runtimes and none for Vibe, though the Vibe row's document line is the mechanism that answers the table's question for a runtime with no command loader.\n    Finding class: doc_code_drift\n    Scope proof: The hook contract is a declared scope file and the Vibe row is the changed line; the handler and part it describes are in scope.\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":3}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/iterations/iteration-003.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"1. **The Vibe row ignores the hook's `match` filter, so an entry scoped away from the main agent still reads `ok vibe`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` -- `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command` from each `[[hooks]]` block, and `inspect` accepts a block whose type is `pre_agent` and whose command ends with the marker. Vibe's own file pairs `match = \\\"main\\\"` with its turn-start and turn-end hooks, which is the evidence that the field scopes the hook to the main agent; the check never reads it.\\n   Finding class: false_pass_diagnostic\\n   Scope proof: The check and its test are declared scope files; the `.vibe/hooks.toml` field values and the README claim are read to test whether the check reports what it says it reports.\\n   Affected surface hints: doctor hook-wiring check, Vibe prompt entry, target-repository diagnostics.\\n   Case: A `.vibe/hooks.toml` block with `type = \\\"pre_agent\\\"`, a `match` value other than the main-agent form (the file already uses `agents_spawn`, `re:write_file|edit` and `ask_user_question` on other hooks) and the turn-start command prints `ok vibe` and exits 0, while the main prompt gets no turn-start. The filter semantics are an inference from the tracked file's pairing of `match = \\\"main\\\"` with both turn hooks; the check's own contract is that it never reads the field.\\n   Evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` (the `type|command` regex), `:253-255` (the filter), `:350-361` (the toml branch), `.vibe/hooks.toml:18` and `:28` (`match = \\\"main\\\"` on the turn hooks) against `:84`, `:92` and `:135` (other match values), `README.markdown:112` (the claim that the check reports whether the prompt entry is wired).\",\"oldString\":\"1. **The Vibe row ignores the hook's `match` filter, so an entry Vibe never runs on a main turn still reads `ok vibe`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` -- `tomlCommands` captures only `type` and `command` from each `[[hooks]]` block, and `inspect` accepts a block whose type is `pre_agent` and whose command ends with the marker. Vibe's own file proves `match` is a real filter on this event family, and a `match` value other than `main` means turn-start does not run for the main agent.\\n   Finding class: false_pass_diagnostic\\n   Scope proof: The check and its test are declared scope files; the `.vibe/hooks.toml` field values and the README claim are read to test whether the check reports what it says it reports.\\n   Affected surface hints: doctor hook-wiring check, Vibe prompt entry, target-repository diagnostics.\\n   Case: A `.vibe/hooks.toml` block with `type = \\\"pre_agent\\\"`, `match = \\\"agents_spawn\\\"` and `command = \\\"node \\\\\\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.skilled/hooks/session-lifecycle/vibe/turn-start.mjs\\\\\\\"\\\"` prints `ok vibe` and exits 0, while Vibe launches turn-start only for the agents-spawn event and the main prompt gets no brief.\\n   Evidence: `hook-wiring-check.cjs:249` (the `type|command` regex), `:253-255` (the filter), `:350-361` (the toml branch), `.vibe/hooks.toml:18` (`match = \\\"main\\\"` on turn-start) and `:84` (`match = \\\"agents_spawn\\\"` on another hook), `README.markdown:112` (the claim that the chec