{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762675600,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0310b64001Qev7j7I5F2JqkG","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeHQJCqAmpoKpkZG","messageID":"msg_1e030c99c001uNmJ4GnV9q5vT6","type":"tool","id":"call_abe5652baba64539b6c7d778","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"### Deviations\n\n- **Coverage graph seed skipped.** The init step that upserts the coverage graph writes through `upsert.cjs` into the spec folder's graph store, which is outside this lineage's write authority. The lineage therefore ran graphless (`graphCoverageMode: graphless_fallback`) and stopped at the iteration cap, a terminal stop that needs no graph decision. The reducer's `graphConvergenceScore` is 0 and the dashboard's graph section is empty.\n- **Resource-map emission skipped.** No root `resource-map.md` exists for this target, the config records `resource_map_present: false`, and the fan-out merge is parent-owned; the lineage report carries no Resource Map Coverage Gate section.\n- **`match` filter semantics** are an inference from the tracked `.vibe/hooks.toml` pairing of `match = \"main\"` with both turn hooks; the verified part of R3-P2-001 is that the check never reads the field.\n\n### Sources Reviewed","oldString":"### Sources Reviewed","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\n@@ -195,8 +195,14 @@\n \n - **R1-P2-001's registered claim named the current no-brief fallback as its input.** The current handler always renders a status head before its directives (`render.ts:655-663`), so that part of the claim was too broad. The defect was re-probed at synthesis against the directive-only shape the module's own `reduceRepeatedHead` supports (`prompt-advisor.mjs:174-177`), where it reproduces; the finding's id, P2 severity and count are unchanged. The delta and ledger claim is append-only and still carries the broader wording, so this report is the corrected adjudication.\n - The same re-probe confirms the headed fallback (`Advisor: no skill matched.\\nDirectives: ...`) is unchanged by `withCommandDocuments`.\n \n+### Deviations\n+\n+- **Coverage graph seed skipped.** The init step that upserts the coverage graph writes through `upsert.cjs` into the spec folder's graph store, which is outside this lineage's write authority. The lineage therefore ran graphless (`graphCoverageMode: graphless_fallback`) and stopped at the iteration cap, a terminal stop that needs no graph decision. The reducer's `graphConvergenceScore` is 0 and the dashboard's graph section is empty.\n+- **Resource-map emission skipped.** No root `resource-map.md` exists for this target, the config records `resource_map_present: false`, and the fan-out merge is parent-owned; the lineage report carries no Resource Map Coverage Gate section.\n+- **`match` filter semantics** are an inference from the tracked `.vibe/hooks.toml` pairing of `match = \"main\"` with both turn hooks; the verified part of R3-P2-001 is that the check never reads the field.\n+\n ### Sources Reviewed\n \n - Scoped code and tests: `review/review-scope-5.txt` lines 3-48 filtered to `vibe-hooks-doctor`.\n - The pass-five brief and focus: `review/review-brief-5.txt`, `review/review-focus-5.txt`.\n","status":"modified","additions":6,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"### Deviations\\n\\n- **Coverage graph seed skipped.** The init step that upserts the coverage graph writes through `upsert.cjs` into the spec folder's graph store, which is outside this lineage's write authority. The lineage therefore ran graphless (`graphCoverageMode: graphless_fallback`) and stopped at the iteration cap, a terminal stop that needs no graph decision. The reducer's `graphConvergenceScore` is 0 and the dashboard's graph section is empty.\\n- **Resource-map emission skipped.** No root `resource-map.md` exists for this target, the config records `resource_map_present: false`, and the fan-out merge is parent-owned; the lineage report carries no Resource Map Coverage Gate section.\\n- **`match` filter semantics** are an inference from the tracked `.vibe/hooks.toml` pairing of `match = \\\"main\\\"` with both turn hooks; the verified part of R3-P2-001 is that the check never reads the field.\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\",\"oldString\":\"### Sources Reviewed\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/vibe-hooks-doctor-5/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794762672996,"end":1794762675600}}}}
